### Food Delivery Platform - Catalog Service
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
### Prerequisite: run restaurant-service.http first, so the owner below has a restaurant
### (it must be ACTIVE for the customer menu in step 12).
###
### Caller identity: the access token of a sign-in below (Authorization: Bearer); its role must be
###   RESTAURANT_ADMIN for /restaurants/mine/**, PLATFORM_ADMIN for /admin/**

@gateway = http://localhost:8080

@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123
@ownerEmail = arjun.spicehub@example.com
@ownerPassword = Owner1234

# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@ownerToken = {{ownerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@restaurantId = {{myRestaurants.response.body.$[0].id}}
@itemId = {{createBiryani.response.body.$.id}}
@itemVersion = {{readItem.response.body.$.version}}
@newCategoryId = {{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}

# Seeded category ids (Flyway V4): 1 Pizza, 2 Burgers, 3 Biryani, 4 Chinese,
# 5 South Indian, 6 North Indian, 7 Desserts, 8 Beverages


### ============================ CUSTOMERS ============================

### 1. Food categories (active, in display order)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/categories


### ============================ OWNER: MENU ============================

### 2. Log in as the restaurant owner -> ownerToken
# @name ownerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{ownerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{ownerPassword}}"
}

### 3. My restaurants -> restaurantId (first one)
# @name myRestaurants
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 4. Add a dish -> itemId
# @name createBiryani
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Chicken Dum Biryani",
  "description": "Slow-cooked Hyderabadi dum biryani with raita",
  "price": 299.00,
  "categoryId": 3,
  "foodType": "NON_VEG",
  "imageUrl": "https://images.example.com/spice-hub/chicken-biryani.jpg",
  "ingredients": "Basmati rice, chicken, curd, spices",
  "nutritionInfo": "Calories 450 kcal, Protein 20 g"
}

### 5. Add more dishes
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Veg Biryani", "price": 219.00, "categoryId": 3, "foodType": "VEG" }

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Double Ka Meetha", "price": 129.00, "categoryId": 7, "foodType": "VEG" }

###
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Egg Biryani", "price": 189.00, "categoryId": 3, "foodType": "EGG" }

### 6. Same dish name again (409)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Chicken Dum Biryani", "price": 279.00, "categoryId": 3, "foodType": "NON_VEG" }

### 7. My whole menu (every status), ordered by category
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 8. Read one item -> itemVersion (run before steps 9 and 10)
# @name readItem
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 9. Change the price (with the version you read)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{itemId}}/price
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 319.00, "version": {{itemVersion}} }

### 10. Same request again with the old version (409, optimistic locking)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{itemId}}/price
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 289.00, "version": {{itemVersion}} }

### 11. Sold out for today (stays on the menu, greyed out)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{itemId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "available": false }

### 12. Customer menu: grouped by category, sold-out items have available=false
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu

### 13. Back in stock
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{itemId}}/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "available": true }

### 14. Hide the item from the menu, then show it again
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{itemId}}/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

###
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{itemId}}/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


### ======================== ADMIN: CATEGORIES ========================

### 15. Log in as the platform admin -> adminToken
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 16. All categories with how many menu items use each
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 17. Create a category (goes to the end of the order) -> newCategoryId
# @name createCategory
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rolls & Wraps",
  "description": "Kathi rolls, shawarma and wraps"
}

### 18. Rename it
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{newCategoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rolls",
  "description": "Kathi rolls and wraps"
}

### 19. Reorder: every category id once, in the new order (new category second)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories/order
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "categoryIds": [3, {{newCategoryId}}, 1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8] }

### 20. A category in use cannot be deleted (409): Biryani has items
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories/3?reason=Test
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 21. Deactivate the new category (hidden from customers, cannot be chosen for items)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{newCategoryId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Not launching rolls this quarter" }

### 22. Delete the unused category (204)
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{newCategoryId}}?reason=Created%20by%20mistake
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 23. Category audit history (kept even after deletion)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{newCategoryId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ======================== ADMIN: MENU ITEMS ========================

### 24. Items of one restaurant
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items?restaurantId={{restaurantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 25. Price review: expensive items first
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items?minPrice=250&sort=price,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 26. Availability review: everything sold out right now
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items?available=false
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 26a. Add an item to any restaurant (listed and available, same rules as the owner)
# @name adminCreateItem
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "restaurantId": {{restaurantId}}, "name": "Admin Special Biryani", "price": 349.00, "categoryId": 3, "foodType": "NON_VEG" }

### 26b. Edit it (send the version you last read; status and availability stay)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/{{adminCreateItem.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Admin Special Biryani", "price": 369.00, "categoryId": 3, "foodType": "NON_VEG", "version": {{adminCreateItem.response.body.$.version}} }

### 26c. Duplicate it (the copy is DISABLED, named "... (copy)")
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/{{adminCreateItem.response.body.$.id}}/duplicate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 26d. Categories with the most items and their orderable share (limit 1..12, default 3)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/category-stats?limit=3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 27. Block an item (the owner cannot re-enable it)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/{{itemId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Photo does not match the dish" }

### 28. Owner tries to enable it (422)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/mine/{{restaurantId}}/menu-items/{{itemId}}/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 29. Admin releases it
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/{{itemId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Owner uploaded a correct photo" }

### 30. Move an item to another category
PUT {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/{{itemId}}/category
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "categoryId": 6, "reason": "Testing a category move" }

### 31. Removing a live (ACTIVE) item is refused (409): block it first
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/{{itemId}}?reason=Test
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 32. Item audit history
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/{{itemId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ======================= EVENTS (Kafka, Phase 7) =======================
### catalog-service keeps its own copy of each restaurant (owner, name, status) from RestaurantChanged
### events, so menus keep working while restaurant-service is down. Try it:
###   docker compose stop restaurant-service
###   run the request below (still 200), then: docker compose start restaurant-service
### Events that fail twice go to fooddelivery.restaurant.changed.DLT (see Kafka UI http://localhost:8090).

### Customer menu, served without calling restaurant-service
### Since Phase 12 it is also cached in Redis: the first read builds it from MySQL, the next ones come from Redis,
### and any change to the menu, the restaurant or the categories is visible on the very next read.
### See the cached copies: docker exec -it fd-redis redis-cli --scan --pattern "catalog:v1:*"
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/menu

### Since Phase 11 catalog-service also publishes, through its transactional outbox, for search-service:
###   MenuItemChanged  (fooddelivery.catalog.menu-item-changed, key = menuItemId): CREATED, UPDATED, PRICE_CHANGED,
###                    AVAILABILITY_CHANGED, STATUS_CHANGED, CATEGORY_CHANGED, REMOVED
###   CategoryChanged  (fooddelivery.catalog.category-changed, key = categoryId): CREATED, UPDATED, STATUS_CHANGED,
###                    REORDERED, DELETED
### Each event carries the current state and version. To fill (or rebuild) the search index with everything that
### already exists in MySQL, replay the current state as REPUBLISHED events (audited, changes no data):

### Republish every category
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/categories/events/republish
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Republish every menu item
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/admin/menu-items/events/republish
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### MenuItemChanged schema in Schema Registry
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.catalog.menu-item-changed-value/versions/latest

### ========================= OPERATIONS =========================

### Health (direct)
GET http://localhost:8083/actuator/health

### Swagger UI: http://localhost:8083/swagger-ui.html
GET http://localhost:8083/v3/api-docs
